Seminormalization -- a package used to seminormalize rings
**********************************************************

Description
===========

Seminormalization is a package which can be used to seminormalize rings or more
generally check if a ring is seminormal.  Roughly speaking a ring is non-normal
if in the Spec, points are identified and tangent spaces killed.  Seminormal
rings are those where only points are identified.  See the following for more
discussion: MathOverflow question (see
https://mathoverflow.net/questions/109395/is-there-a-geometric-intuition-
underlying-the-notion-of-normal-varieties/ )

Core functions
  * *note seminormalize: seminormalize, computes the seminormalization of a
    ring
  * *note isSeminormal: isSeminormal, checks if a ring is seminormal
To accomplish this, this we first normalize the ring via *note integralClosure:
(IntegralClosure)integralClosure, and then glue points together via the *note
Pullback: (Pullback)Top, package.  There are some other functions exported
which people may also find useful.

Other useful functions
  * *note ringProduct: ringProduct, finds a ring equal to a product of rings
  * *note betterNormalizationMap: betterNormalizationMap, computes the integral
    closure of reduced rings (that are not necessarily domains)

