betterNormalizationMap -- normalizes non domains
************************************************

  * Usage: 
        phi = betterNormalizationMap(S)
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Strategy: betterNormalizationMap_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmStrategy=>_pd_pd_
        pd_rp, => ..., default value {}, controls what strategy is used in
        calls to integralClosure
      * *note Variable: seminormalize_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVariable=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value Yy, set the name for new variables created by the
        function
  * Outputs:
      * phi, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, the map from the ring to
        its normalization

Description
===========

Given a reduced ring $S$, this returns the normalization map $S \to S^N$.  It
works by computing the normalization after modding out by each minimal prime,
and then taking the product of the rings.  This should be compared to the
function icMap built into Macaulay2.

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y]/ideal(x*y);                           |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : icMap(R);                                         |
|                                                       |
|o2 : RingMap R <-- R                                   |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : h2 = betterNormalizationMap(R);                   |
|                                                       |
|                       QQ[Yy0, Yy1, Yy2]               |
|o3 : RingMap ------------------------------------ <-- R|
|                 2                                     |
|             (Yy2  - Yy2, Yy1*Yy2 - Yy1, Yy0*Yy2)      |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : RN = target h2                                    |
|                                                       |
|o4 = RN                                                |
|                                                       |
|o4 : QuotientRing                                      |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : radical ideal singularLocus RN                    |
|                                                       |
|o5 = ideal 1                                           |
|                                                       |
|o5 : Ideal of QQ[Yy0, Yy1, Yy2]                        |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

