conductorOfRingMap -- given a ring map this finds the conductor of the map
**************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        J = conductorOfRingMap phi
  * Inputs:
      * phi, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * J, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the conductor

Description
===========

Given a ring map $\phi : R \to S$, this finds the conductor, the annihilator of
$S/R$ as an $R$ module.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a,b]/ideal(a^3-b^2);|
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : S = QQ[c];                 |
+--------------------------------+
|i3 : phi = map(S, R, {c^2,c^3});|
|                                |
|o3 : RingMap S <-- R            |
+--------------------------------+
|i4 : conductorOfRingMap phi     |
|                                |
|o4 = ideal (b, a)               |
|                                |
|o4 : Ideal of R                 |
+--------------------------------+

Ways to use conductorOfRingMap:
===============================

  * "conductorOfRingMap(RingMap)"

